Package: modelly
Title: Agent-Based Models with 'Modelly' from R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Remi", "Pelloux", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "rp@openpro.ai")
Description: Run, sweep and calibrate agent-based models written with the
    'Modelly' Python framework <https://github.com/RemiPelloux/Modelly> from R.
    Results come back as data frames; calibration by approximate Bayesian
    computation (ABC-SMC) returns posterior summaries and particles.
    'Modelly' runs in Python through 'reticulate'; install_modelly() sets it up.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
URL: https://remipelloux.github.io/Modelly/dev/r_and_julia.html
BugReports: https://github.com/RemiPelloux/Modelly/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    reticulate (>= 1.30)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.12) with the modelly-abm package (>= 1.5)
